---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
---
<Docs title="Vue — Matra docs" description="useEditor and EditorContent for Vue 3, first-class rather than community-maintained." section="Frameworks" heading="Vue">
  <pre><code>npm i @matrajs/core @matrajs/vue</code></pre>
  <p>
    Vue is first-class here rather than a community package that lags the React one. Both
    bindings are written together and released together.
  </p>

  <h2>An editor</h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;script setup&gt;
import &#123; starterKit &#125; from '@matrajs/core'
import &#123; EditorContent, useEditor &#125; from '@matrajs/vue'

const editor = useEditor(&#123;
  extensions: starterKit,
  content: '&lt;p&gt;Hello.&lt;/p&gt;',
&#125;)
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;EditorContent :editor="editor" /&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>The editor is destroyed automatically when the component unmounts.</p>

  <h2>A toolbar</h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;script setup&gt;
import &#123; useEditorState &#125; from '@matrajs/vue'

const props = defineProps(['editor'])
const characters = useEditorState(props.editor, (e) =&gt; e.getText().length)
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;button @mousedown.prevent="editor.commands.toggleBold()"&gt;Bold&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;span&gt;&#123;&#123; characters &#125;&#125;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;</code></pre>

  <div class="note">
    <code>@mousedown.prevent</code> rather than <code>@click</code>. A click moves focus to
    the button first and collapses the selection, so the command runs against a caret instead
    of the words that were highlighted.
  </div>
</Docs>
